{
  "name": "Harmony Touch 7.1, switching between activities",
  "summary": "One activity to the next: the new power ons first, then the old power offs, the Denon kept on.",
  "description": "On the bench Harmony Touch holding work/touch-firmware/sets/6.9-label-back (the recorded full sync's documents under tags of ours, as put back by the own set and the changed set). Every expectation is derived from those documents by packages/bench/src/touchengine.ts, a model of the engine read in the firmware, and named as the monitor names a code of the Touch's own documents. Step 1 presses Off so no activity runs and the engine holds every device off; what it sends depends on what ran before and is not judged. Each activity is started while another runs. Predicted: the old activity's end steps that are not power offs first (from Switch Box the LG TV's Mute), then the new activity's power ons, but only for devices the engine holds off, then the old activity's power offs for devices the new one does not use, then the new inputs. The Denon is kept on between activities (IsPoweredOnBetweenActivities), so leaving an activity for one without it does not switch it off; only Off does. An input is sent every time, even when the device is already on it. Wait for the codes to stop before pressing Next: an activity start runs about 15 seconds, most of it the LG TV's 10 second power on delay.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "instruction": "Button: Off"
    },
    {
      "instruction": "Activity: Watch TV",
      "expect": [
        {
          "device": "LG TV",
          "command": "PowerOn"
        },
        {
          "device": "Denon AV Receiver",
          "command": "PowerOn",
          "pauseMs": [
            700,
            1250
          ]
        },
        {
          "device": "Denon AV Receiver",
          "command": "InputTVAudio",
          "pauseMs": [
            3750,
            4350
          ]
        },
        {
          "device": "LG TV",
          "command": "InputHdmi1",
          "pauseMs": [
            5000,
            5600
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "instruction": "Activity: Switch Box",
      "expect": [
        {
          "device": "KPN",
          "command": "PowerToggle"
        },
        {
          "device": "Switch",
          "command": "PowerOn",
          "pauseMs": [
            1550,
            2100
          ]
        },
        {
          "device": "LG TV",
          "command": "InputHdmi3",
          "pauseMs": [
            550,
            1100
          ]
        },
